{"chunk_id": "8b7d4eb5cae4", "text": "After Ravana\u2019s defeat, Rama shocks the gathered hosts by rejecting Sita, declaring he fought the war only to restore his honor, not out of attachment to her. He suggests she may go to another protector, implying her time in Ravana\u2019s captivity has tainted her. The accusation devastates Sita. In front of the assembled warriors, she laments the injustice, insisting her heart has always remained faithful and that any contact with Ravana occurred against her will. She reproaches Rama for doubting her despite her proven devotion and the suffering endured to rescue her. Concluding that public shame leaves her no other recourse, she commands Lakshmana to prepare a funeral pyre so she may prove her purity through fire. As Rama stands stern and silent, Lakshmana reluctantly obeys and Sita approaches the flames, invoking the gods before the ordeal.\nRama harshly questions Sita\u2019s purity after rescuing her, prompting her sorrowful defense and decision to prove her chastity through a trial by fire.\nThemes: honor and chastity, public shame, trial by fire, marital conflict, dharma and reputation", "vector": [0.014456983655691147, -0.027699094265699387, -0.009847217239439487, 0.002584978938102722, -0.017332181334495544, 0.00427567632868886, -0.025296347215771675, 0.010150935500860214, -0.0328555554151535, -0.015577365644276142, 0.018655043095350266, 0.014996927231550217, 0.02088231034576893, 0.014645963907241821, -0.010177932679653168, -0.0012899584835395217, 0.05153759568929672, 0.002225578995421529, 0.029615893959999084, -0.016117310151457787, -0.020814817398786545, -0.018439065665006638, -0.013417592272162437, 0.02572830207645893, -0.029372919350862503, -0.009347769431769848, 0.020558344200253487, -0.03444838523864746, 0.014726955443620682, -0.011568286456167698, -0.02028837241232395, -0.015914831310510635, -0.018317578360438347, -0.015698853880167007, -0.03442138805985451, -0.013606572523713112, -0.007795432116836309, -0.0268